From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:16:18 +0000
Subject: fix(compose): guard lazy scroll against native echoes of programmatic
 moves

Classify each native scroll callback while a programmatic offset move is
pending: the exact echo is consumed (and restores the move's target into
composeOffset), any other callback only syncs composeOffset, and a user
drag releases the guard and is dispatched. The guard stays armed until
the echo, a drag, or a 1s timeout for lost or clamped echoes.

Upstream swallowed every callback until an exact match and could freeze
on a lost echo; a one-shot guard instead let Android top overscroll and
bounce callbacks disarm it before a deferred >= 3000dp top expansion
echoed, so the echo was dispatched as a user scroll and short lists
jumped to their end.

Fork-Patch: compose-scroll-echo-guards
Origin: 996a20fd, 2527b9ec
Upstream-Status: pending
Signed-off-by: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>

